# Radar parent grouping

Home and Radar may present the same rows differently. Do not “fix” Radar by copying Home’s standalone cards.

## Grouping

- **2+** open watch children → one parent card (`asRadarWatchCards`) when that cluster is **not** already on Home. Far-week packing still groups this way.
- Parent may be obligation, hold, context_only, or occurrence — not only calendar events.
- If Home already shows the needed-now cluster (gala + form + kit), Radar must **not** repeat it. `exceptHomeActions` drops that parent group.
- Single watch child may stay its own card. Undated buy-child of a **hold** must not — hide it; the hold is the card.
- Never children of a dismissed/done parent (including when the parent is missing from the open query). Never a Card/Present/Gift title as its own card.

## Home vs kit

- This-week event + form/RSVP + kit → one Home card. Kit is not a second Radar group of the same event.
- Far event: form/RSVP may still be a standalone Home card; leftover packing can group on Radar.
- Invented interview prep (research / examples / JD) is not Home. If the occurrence is dismissed, it is not Radar either.

## Tests

`lib/placement.selftest.ts`: this-week gala and farm slip are one Home card each, packing not competing as extra Home cards, Radar does not duplicate the cluster. Do not delete those assertions.
